  "lineage": "Sfyria whistled-language tradition of Antia village on Mount Ochi in Evia island, Greece — a fully grammatical whistled register of the Greek language using turbulent lip-and-tongue-formed source to encode Greek phonemes across the mountain-and-canyon terrain of Mount Ochi; documented by the contemporary linguistic-anthropology lineage including Sotiris Apostolopoulos and the Onassis Foundation cultural-preservation initiatives; the smaller and more endangered sibling of Silbo Gomero, with only a handful of remaining fluent speakers in the Antia village; the whistled-language family includes the Kuşköy Turkish Black Sea whistled-Turkish tradition, the Hmong courtship-whistle, Mazatec, and other documented whistled-languages globally",
